```

The `/yy[*]` block has no `layout`, so its default (vertical, because the yy box is wider than
tall after children are measured) stacks rows. Note the `[*]` parse-scope syntax reopens a scope
declared earlier as `/m5_YY_HIER` (i.e. `/yy[9:0]`).

sort_viz uses `this.getIndex("level")` to compute a per-column pipeline offset and then
`'$in_num'.step(level)` so each column shows the value as it was `level` cycles earlier, a typical
"unroll the pipeline in space" trick.

