### 15.2 Channel contract **[IDE source]**

`PWA` opens its own result panes with a contract object under `options.channel`:

```
ide.openThirdPartyPane(mnemonic, "iframe", {contentUrl: ...},
  {channel: {subscribes: [{type: "compile-result", sources: ["ide"]},
                          {type: "theme",          sources: ["ide"]}],
             rpc: true}})
```

`PANE` shows `Pane._initChannel(options)` creating `new PaneChannel(pane, iframeEl, ide.bus,
options.channel ?? {})` only when `contentType === "iframe"`; `PaneChannel` wraps a
`BusParticipant(mnemonic, bus, contract, {send, onRpcRequest})`, listens to `window` `message`
events whose `event.source` is the pane iframe's `contentWindow`, forwards `event.data` to
`participant.receive`, posts outbound messages with `iframe.contentWindow.postMessage(msg, "*")`,
and serves RPC only for target `"ide"` via `ide.callPaneRpc(pane, method, args)` (any other target
throws "Unsupported RPC target"). The iframe sandbox is `allow-scripts allow-same-origin
allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox`.

### 15.3 Pane side, raw postMessage v1 (VIEWS: news_feed, pomodoro, games)

Messages carry `v: 1`. Verbatim from `news_feed.html`:

```
window.addEventListener("message", (e) => {
  const m = e.data;
  if (!m || typeof m !== "object" || m.v !== PANE_V) return;
  if (m.kind === "rpc-result") { _rpcPending.get(m.id)?.resolve(m.result); _rpcPending.delete(m.id); }
  else if (m.kind === "rpc-error") { _rpcPending.get(m.id)?.reject(new Error(m.error)); _rpcPending.delete(m.id); }
});

function callIde(method, ...args) {
  const id = ++_rpcSeq;
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    if (window.parent === window) { reject(new Error("not a pane")); return; }
    _rpcPending.set(id, { resolve, reject });
    parent.postMessage({ v: PANE_V, kind: "rpc", id, target: "ide", method, args }, "*");
  });
}
...
    try { parent.postMessage({ v: PANE_V, type: "ready" }, "*"); } catch (_) {}
    try {
      const ctx = await callIdeTimeout("getContext", [], 1500);
      if (ctx?.theme) applyTheme(!!ctx.theme.dark);
    } catch (_) { /* non-Makerchip host */ }
```

So the observed message shapes are: pane -> IDE `{v: 1, type: "ready"}` (handshake), pane -> IDE
`{v: 1, kind: "rpc", id, target: "ide", method, args}`, IDE -> pane `{v: 1, kind: "rpc-result",
id, result}` or `{v: 1, kind: "rpc-error", id, error}`. The subscription (`ext/<type>`) delivery
shape and the host-to-pane RPC request shape were not observable locally.

Pane-callable methods seen: `getContext` (returns `{theme: {dark}}`; **[example-only]**, not in
`API_METHODS`), `getAvailablePanes`, `setCode` (GAL). Whether every `IdePlugin` public method is
reachable from a pane is not stated in mirrored docs.

### 15.4 `@rweda/makerchip-view-client` (GAL, verbatim excerpts)

```
import { connect } from "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@rweda/makerchip-view-client@0.2.0/+esm";
...
// connect() finds the parent window when embedded and auto-sends the `ready`
// handshake; in a standalone tab `view.embedded` is false and call() rejects.
const view = connect();

function callIdeWithTimeout(method, args, ms) {
  return Promise.race([
    view.call(method, ...args),
    new Promise((_, reject) => setTimeout(() => reject(new Error("IDE RPC timed out")), ms)),
  ]);
}

async function initPaneMode() {
  if (!view.embedded) return;
  try {
    await callIdeWithTimeout("getAvailablePanes", [], 1500);
  } catch (_) {
    return; // No Makerchip IDE (plain iframe / other embed) -> stay in web mode.
  }
  document.body.classList.add("pane-mode");
  ...
}

async function openInIde(ex, btn) {
  ...
    const code = await res.text();
    // setCode loads the source into the Editor and compiles it; in an editor-less
    // IDE (hasEditor: false) it degrades to a headless compile.
    await view.call("setCode", code);
  ...
}
```

The gallery comment states the protocol is documented in `doc-src/plugin/Third_Party_Pane_API.md`
of the Makerchip mono repo, and that the pane must be opened "with a channel contract that has
`rpc: true`" for `view.call` to work. Only `connect()`, `view.embedded`, and `view.call(method,
...args)` are exercised; no event-subscription API of the client is visible locally.

Standalone loading of these panes: `README.md` says HTML pages in `views/` "can be loaded into a
Makerchip View pane by URL", and the gallery opens examples with
`https://www.makerchip.com/sandbox?code_url=<encoded raw URL>`.

